CountDownLatch

- A bit like semaphore but specialized, it accepts, a counter
- CountDownLatch countDownLatch = new CountDownLatch(counter)
- Provides functionality of decreasing the counter
- countDownLatch.countDown()
- countDownLatch.await() - blocks currently executing thread, when count down reaches 0, await will be unblocked
- mostly used for subproblems executed in parallel, when a sub problem is solved we call countDown marking the fact that 
that one was solved
- We don't have any way of increasing the counter once it reaches 0
- One shot tool

In search a num in array problem, we divide the portions of array to worker threads to search in.
Once the thread completes the work, we call countDown to denote that this thread has completed searching
At the end in main thread, we wait for all threads to complete before printing the search posiion by using await()
Once all threads complete their work, the count down will become 0 and await() will unblock
At that point we can print results.

The idea behind this concept is, when each sub problem is solved, we count down to indicate that the sub problem was solved.
One shot problems that can split into multiple problems that can run in parallel.


Barriers

- CyclicBarrier cyclicBarrier = new CyclicBarrier(num)
- As a barrier, it will block the threads so in constructor we provide number of threads
- cyclicBarrier.await(), after all threads hit the barrier, they will be released by the barrier
and continue the execution
- Idea is simple all threads will reach barrier before they are released for execution. 
- Importantly it can be reused, as the name suggests, it is cyclic in nature and will reset on its own.
- CyclicBarrier cyclicBarrier = new CyclicBarrier(num, runnable) runnable will be called when barrier is released

We solved a problem where we had a 2d matrix, for each cell, we added all elements of previous row + current cell.
Each thread was responsible for updating one column. After updating one cell in that column, we would wait for other threads to update their cells.
Once all threads update, barrier will release and thread will move on to updating the next cell in the column.
Reason why we would need to wait for each thread to complete is because we want to do previous row sum + current cell 

Essentially,
Wait until 4 threads call barrier.await().
Once the 4th thread arrives, release all 4 threads.
Then reset the barrier so it can be used again.


